From 7315d05fdc8748378f58b9006a0c75de410bbde0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:41:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] BananaDS: melonDS patches 0022 (JIT exit stats) and 0023
 (jit.irqchain: masked IRQs don't end block chains)

0022: MELONDS_JIT_EXITSTATS=n prints, per frame from frame n on, why the JIT's block chains came back to the
slice loop (compiles, region setups, IRQs taken, IRQs CPSR.I masks, halts and idle loops), counted on the loop's
cold paths only. 0023: the exit stubs go on into the next block when the only stop reason is an IRQ that CPSR.I
masks (the loop would only call TriggerIRQ, which returns at once). jit.irqchain=off (MELONDS_JIT_NOIRQCHAIN=1)
is the old behaviour; exact either way (pictures, main RAM, audio dump identical on the test ROMs).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PvbFhKAw3ERk5a13S651g1
